# Rebuild lidingobuild/course-model.json where the Lantmäteriet credential is.
#
# build-course.mjs asserts its 1 m raster against a pinned sourceFloat32Sha256,
# and that raster lives in a gitignored cache: rebuild-terrain-raster.mjs
# measures why the published tiles cannot stand in for it - they cover the
# window completely but are QUANTISED, so they give the terrain's shape and not
# the acquisition's bytes, and the pin is a contract about the bytes.
#
# This run must pick up, all of it in one rebuild:
#   - the united sea, 607.75 ha in three rings replacing 9.90 ha of fragments
#     clipped to the terrain window (mapping/coast-rings.geojson)
#   - the eight measured tee decks, which take card marks standing on measured
#     ground from 52 of 90 to 61
#   - hole 13's bunker, the one the club's course council reports building
#   - millimetre output precision, so this machine's PROJ and CI's agree
#   - the 3 m tree-cover raster this ground never had (emit-pack reads
#     lidingobuild/tree-cover.json directly)
#
# It also clears the one known failure on the branch:
# course.node-test's "every published green and physical tee is an observed
# source polygon" fails by sub-millimetre amounts until the model is rebuilt
# from the rounded rings.
